course: dictionary
lesson: 10515
title: Twitch: a small, quick movement
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Twitch can be a verb or a noun. As a verb, to twitch means to make a small, quick movement, often one you do not mean to make. As a noun, a twitch is that small, quick movement itself. «My eye twitched» is the verb; «an eye twitch» is the noun.
explain: You can also twitch something on purpose, like a nose. «The rabbit twitched its nose.» Read the words around twitch: small, quick and nose are the clues. A twitch is never a big or slow movement.
explain: Stories use twitch for people too. «The curtains twitched» means a nosy neighbour is peeking out, so twitch can mean a quick, sly movement. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence: does «the curtains moved a little and quickly» still make sense? If it does, you have it.
fact: To twitch means to make a small, quick movement.
fact: A twitch is a noun: «Each twitch of a muscle» means one small, quick movement of a muscle.
fact: Twitch can be a verb (twitch, twitches, twitched, twitching) or a noun (a twitch, twitches).
fact: «Twitch» can mean a small, quick movement you do not mean to make, like «My eye twitched».
fact: Muscles can twitch on their own, and every twitch sends out a tiny electric signal.
exercise: «The rabbit twitched its nose.» What does twitched mean here? | Ate all the carrots | Sat very still | Hopped far away | *Moved a little, quickly
exercise: «Each heartbeat and each twitch of a muscle sends out a weak electric buzz.» What is a twitch in this sentence? | *A small, quick movement | A loud noise | A type of electric buzz | A long walk
exercise: «Stop stroking a cat when its tail twitches, its skin ripples or its ears turn back.» What does the tail twitch tell you? | *The cat may be ready for you to stop | Stroking makes the tail grow | The cat has fallen asleep | The cat wants a bigger stroke
test: «My eye gave a twitch when I was tired.» In this sentence, what is twitch? | A verb: to hop | A colour | *A noun: a small, quick movement | A place to rest
test: Which sentence uses twitch to mean moving something a little and quickly? | The clock struck twelve. | She ran out of the shop. | *The rabbit twitched its nose. | The sea was calm and still.
exam: «Octopuses have a short active sleep when their arms twitch.» What does twitch mean here? | *Small, quick movements, like a shiver of the arms | Long, slow stretches | Sticking firmly to rocks | Swimming fast in a straight line
